1. Executive Summary
What the current application actually is
The codebase is a client-side React 19 + TypeScript + Vite static UI prototype (src/App.tsx, src/main.tsx). It implements a public landing page (/), 14 public directory/informational pages, client-side localStorage authentication/onboarding flows, and three role-partitioned workspace shells (member, organization, admin).
Maturity
Frontend UI shell: Prototype / visual mockup stage. Build (tsc -b && vite build) and lint (oxlint) succeed, and routing/navigation render cleanly.
Business logic & persistence: Non-existent beyond localStorage user registration/session storage (src/app/AuthProvider.tsx) and ephemeral component-level useState toggles (e.g., bookmark icon state in ListingCard.tsx, unread boolean in NotificationExperience, resolved report titles in ModerationExperience).
Backend / API / Web3: Zero backend server, zero database, zero API client, zero wallet/blockchain integration.
What is already useful
Clean Vite + React 19 + TypeScript + React Router v7 setup (package.json, src/App.tsx).
Semantic route-slug utilities and layout shell structure (src/app/navigation.ts, src/layouts/AppLayout.tsx, src/components/PageScaffold.tsx, src/components/PageHeader.tsx).
Reusable card/stat primitives (ListingCard.tsx, StatCard.tsx, EmptyState.tsx, Brand.tsx) and responsive drawer scrim mechanics (AppLayout.tsx, Sidebar.tsx).
src/types/index.ts and src/lib/utils.ts contain domain helper stubs (though currently orphaned and misaligned with the new spec's XP/CP/House model).
Largest gaps against Specification v1.0
No backend, database, or authoritative ledger: Everything is hardcoded static arrays (src/data/listings.ts, inline arrays in PublicPageExperience.tsx and WorkspaceExperiences.tsx) or localStorage (AuthProvider.tsx).
Incompatible account & role model: Uses 3 mutually exclusive roles (member | organization | admin) with separate registration paths, separate dashboards, and disjoint route gates (AuthGate.tsx), whereas the spec mandates one Arena account/identity, Spartan default membership, Newbie as an onboarding stage, permission-based capabilities (creators/sponsors/reviewers/mentors/Elders/Strategoi/Control Room), and no separate organization account type.
Missing core domain systems:
Houses: None of the 6 Houses (Scribes, Heralds, Artisans, Echoes, Forge Masters, Seers) exist; replaced by generic Web3 "Communities".
Missions & Verification: No Mission entity, creator funding/XP reservation, submission & evidence capture, reviewer approval/rejection/resubmission, dispute resolution, expiry/refunds, or duplicate/fraud prevention.
XP & Contribution Points (CP): No Lifetime vs. Spendable XP split, no auditable XP ledger, no Contribution Points model, no 30 configurable levels, and no 5 Ascendancy ranks.
Product Shell: Navigation has ~28 routes across mismatched categories (Opportunities, Grants, Bounties, Communities, Services, Messages, etc.) instead of the 6 primary destinations (Home, Missions, Houses, Explore, Academy, Events) + Personal area (My Activity, My Profile) + gated Stewardship/Control Room.
Out-of-scope MVP feature present: MessagesExperience (/messages) implements an in-app chat UI, which is explicitly excluded from MVP.
Most important architectural risks
Conflicting CSS layers (index.css + App.css + theme.css): theme.css appends a blanket !important override block (* { font-size: max(.875rem, 1em)!important; background-color: transparent!important; }) over two earlier incompatible themes, breaking typography hierarchy and mobile button layouts.
Unsecured client-side auth & role switching: AuthProvider.tsx trusts localStorage and exposes 1-click admin demo login (AuthForm.tsx).
Orphaned code & dead dependencies: src/data/mockData.ts (1,177 lines), src/types/index.ts, src/lib/utils.ts, 17 @radix-ui/* packages, and framer-motion are completely unused, creating false confidence that features exist.
