5. Authentication, Accounts and Permissions Audit
Current Model (src/app/AuthProvider.tsx, src/app/authContext.ts, src/components/AuthGate.tsx)
Storage & Security: Credentials and sessions are stored unencrypted in browser localStorage (arena.accounts.v1, arena.session.v1) with client-side SHA-256 hashing (hashPassword). Anyone can edit localStorage to set role: "admin" or click the Administrator demo button in AuthForm.tsx:95.
Account Split: Registration (AuthForm.tsx:80-83) requires choosing member or organization. AuthGate.tsx:9 blocks organization users from /profile, /achievements, /notifications, /reputation, /settings (MEMBER_PAGES), and blocks member users from creating opportunities (ORG_PAGES).
Onboarding Bug: AuthProvider.tsx:109-112 (completeOnboarding) updates arena.session.v1 only, leaving arena.accounts.v1 untouched, so name and focus are lost on re-login. Furthermore, onboarding only captures display name and a generic dropdown (intent), not primary/secondary House selection or Newbie stage tracking.
Required Changes for Specification v1.0
Single Arena Account & Identity: Collapse member and organization into one UserAccount entity backed by server-side authentication (HTTP-only session cookies or short-lived JWT + OAuth/email verification). Remove demo role impersonation in production builds.
Membership & Stage Model:
Unauthenticated user = Visitor (read-only access to public pages).
Authenticated user = Spartan by default (membershipStatus: 'spartan').
Onboarding = Newbie stage (onboardingStage: 'newbie' | 'completed' + checklist milestones), not a separate role.
Organizations become entity profiles (OrganizationProfile) owned/managed by permitted Spartan accounts (e.g., sponsors), not separate user login types.
Explicit RBAC + Scoped Permissions: Replace roles={['admin']} in AuthGate with permission claims (e.g., missions.create, missions.review, house.steward scoped to houseId, stewardship.elder, admin.control_room, xp.adjust). Enforce every permission check on the backend API as well as in UI route guards (PermissionGate).
6. Missions and XP Architecture Audit
Current State
Missions: Absent. src/data/listings.ts defines a 10-field Listing type for display cards; src/types/index.ts defines separate Opportunity, Bounty, Grant, Hackathon types (unused). None model mission states, budgets, evidence, or review workflows.
XP & Reputation: Sidebar.tsx (2,450 / 3,000 XP), WorkspaceOverview.tsx (2,450 reputation), Leaderboard (3,840 XP), and ReputationExperience (2,450 REPUTATION POINTS) conflate XP and reputation and hardcode static numbers.
Systems Required by Specification v1.0
A. Mission Lifecycle & Verification Engine
Mission Entity & Types: Support all spec categories (outreach/distribution, creative, writing/research, technical, learning, events/participation, community support, offline, collaboration, custom) with explicit policy validation blocking paid engagement-farming (no incentivized X likes, reposts, replies, follows, or views).
State Machine: Draft -> Funded / Active (XP budget reserved) -> Paused / Cancelled (unused XP refunded) / Expired -> Completed / Settled.
Submission & Evidence Lifecycle:
Duplicate/fraud guard: uniqueness constraint (missionId, applicantId) per allowed attempt, evidence URL/file hash checks, rate limiting, and eligibility checks (House/level/Spartan status).
Submission states: Submitted -> Under Review -> Approved (triggers atomic settlement) OR Changes Requested / Rejected (allows resubmission up to configurable limit) OR Disputed (escalates to Steward/Control Room).
Reviewer Assignment: Creator-designated reviewers, House Strategoi/Elders, or verification rules, with conflict-of-interest checks (reviewer cannot approve own submission).
B. Dual-Balance XP, Ledger & Contribution Points Architecture
Dual XP Balances (derived or transactionally maintained):
lifetimeXp: Monotonically increasing cumulative earned XP. Used for 30 configurable levels. Spending/allocating XP never reduces lifetimeXp.
spendableXp: Available XP for funding missions or permitted Arena services.
Append-Only Auditable XP Ledger (xp_ledger_entries):
Immutable entries with id, userId, type (EARN | RESERVE | SPEND_ALLOCATE | RECEIVE | REFUND | ADMIN_ADJUSTMENT), deltaLifetime, deltaSpendable, referenceType (mission | submission | activity | admin), referenceId, actorId, reason, idempotencyKey, and createdAt.
Mission funding atomically decrements spendableXp into a mission escrow/reservation (RESERVE). Approvals settle from reserved pool to contributor (RECEIVE), and cancellations/expiries return unspent escrow (REFUND).
Contribution Points (contribution_ledger_entries):
Completely separate from XP (spendableXp / lifetimeXp).
Non-spendable, non-transferable, and drives Seasonal and All-Time Leaderboards.
Progression & Ascendancy:
30 Levels: Driven by configurable level_configs table/thresholds against lifetimeXp.
5 Ascendancy Ranks: Explicit status/rank model distinct from House membership and leadership permissions; leadership appointments (Elder, Strategos, etc.) require explicit administrative grant, never automatic XP triggers.
