10. Recommended Target Architecture
Existing vs. Proposed Infrastructure
Existing (Retain & Refactor): React 19 + TypeScript + Vite SPA (src/), React Router v7 (App.tsx), layout primitives (AppLayout, PageScaffold, PageHeader, StatCard, EmptyState, ListingCard), and Radix UI primitives already in package.json (dialog, tabs, dropdown-menu, select, tooltip) for accessible modals, tabs, and drawers.
Proposed (New Infrastructure Required):
Backend + Relational Database: Express/Node.js API server (or Next.js/Express server.ts serving Vite in dev and dist/ in production) backed by a transactional relational SQL database (e.g., PostgreSQL via Cloud SQL + Drizzle/Prisma ORM). A relational ACID database is essential for atomic XP escrow reservations, immutable ledger appends, and uniqueness constraints against duplicate submissions.
Object/Evidence Storage: Signed upload storage (or validated URL + attachment metadata) for mission evidence deliverables.
Target Architecture by Domain
Application Shell & Navigation (AppLayout, Sidebar, Topbar):
One unified shell across Visitor, Spartan, Elder/Strategos, and Control Room users.
Collapsible desktop sidebar + mobile left slide-over drawer (auto-closes on route change; also accessible on / mobile). No bottom mobile nav.
Primary nav: Home (/ or /home), Missions (/missions), Houses (/houses), Explore (/explore), Academy (/academy), Events (/events).
Personal nav (authenticated): My Activity (/activity), My Profile (/profile).
Utility & gated access: Global Search (⌘K command modal), Notifications popover + page, Leaderboards (/leaderboards), XP/CP summary pill, Stewardship (/stewardship, permission-gated), Control Room (/control-room, permission-gated).
Authentication & Permissions (auth_sessions, users, permissions, user_permissions):
Server-issued HTTP-only session cookies (email/password + optional OAuth/wallet linking later).
Single users record per person with membershipStatus (spartan), onboardingStage (newbie | active), primaryHouseId, secondaryHouseIds[], ascendancyRankId, lifetimeXp, spendableXp, contributionPoints.
Scoped permissions: mission.create, mission.sponsor, mission.review, stewardship.access (with optional houseId scope for Strategoi), control_room.access, ledger.adjust, config.manage.
User & Organization Profiles (organization_profiles, organization_members):
Organizations/sponsors are first-class entity profiles linked to one or more Spartan accounts with sponsor / manager permissions—not separate login accounts.
Houses (houses, house_memberships):
Seeded with the 6 canonical Houses: Scribes, Heralds, Artisans, Echoes, Forge Masters, Seers.
Single parameterized House page (/houses/:slug) with internal tabs (Overview, Missions, Members, Academy/Resources, Activity).
Echoes outreach/distribution missions support cross-House eligibility flags so Spartans in any House can participate.
Missions, Evidence & Review (missions, mission_submissions, mission_disputes):
Full lifecycle (draft, funded, active, paused, expired, cancelled, completed) with policy guard rejecting prohibited engagement-farming templates.
Submissions capture structured evidence (links, deliverables, notes, metadata hashes), enforce duplicate/rate-limit rules, and support pending_review -> approved | changes_requested | rejected -> disputed.
XP Ledger, Contribution Points & Progression (xp_ledger, cp_ledger, level_configs, ascendancy_ranks, achievements, user_achievements):
All XP mutations execute inside DB transactions updating cached lifetime_xp / spendable_xp projections alongside immutable xp_ledger rows (EARN, RESERVE, ALLOCATE, RECEIVE, REFUND, ADJUST).
cp_ledger records non-spendable Contribution Points feeding Seasonal (seasons table) and All-Time leaderboards.
level_configs stores the 30 configurable levels; ascendancy_ranks stores the 5 ranks (explicitly decoupled from automatic leadership grants).
Events & Academy (events, event_registrations, academy_tracks, academy_lessons, lesson_progress):
Separate Events module with RSVP/attendance verification (can trigger Mission/CP/XP rewards).
Academy structured into tracks/modules/lessons linked to Houses and beginner Newbie onboarding.
Stewardship & Control Room:
Stewardship Workspace: House-scoped queue for Strategoi and Elders (submission reviews, disputes, House health, mentorship/stewardship tasks).
Control Room: Platform-wide configuration (30 levels, activity rewards, achievements, seasons), user permission grants, global dispute escalation, and audited manual XP/CP adjustments.
Styling & Responsive UI:
Remove src/theme.css !important overrides and conflicting App.css/index.css duplication. Standardize on Tailwind CSS + clean CSS variables in a single token layer, using mobile-first responsive grids (min-w-0, no fixed-pixel multi-column row traps).
